{title: 115 - O Come, O Come, Immanuel}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #115 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 115}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Em]O come, [G/D]Ocome, [C]Immanuel, [G]And [Dm]ransom [G/B]captive [Am/C]Is rael
[Bm]That mourns [Em]in [Am]lonely [Em/G]ex ile here [Am]Until [Dm]the Son [Em]of [Dm]Godappear
[G/B]Rejoice! [Am]Rejoice! [Dm]Immanuel Shall [Em]come [Bm]to [G]thee, [C]O [Am]Is [G/B]rael!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Dm]Rejoice! [Em]Rejoice!
[Dm]Emmanuel [C]shall [G/B]come [Am/C]to thee,
[Bm]O Israel.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Em]O [G/D]come, Thou [Am]Wisdom [G]from [C]on [Am/C]high,
[Bm]And [Em]order all things [Am]far [Em]and [Bm]night;
[Bm]To [Em]us [Am]the [Em/G]path of [Am]knowledge [Bm]show,
[G/B]And [C]cause [G/B]us in [Dm]her [Em]ways [G]to [Am]go.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Em]O [G/D]come, Desire of nations, [Am/C]bind
[Bm]In [Em]one [Am]the [Em/G]hearts of [Am]all [Em]mankind;
[Bm]Bid [Em]Thou [Am]our [Em/G]sad divisions [Bm]cease,
[G/B]And [C]be [G/B]Thyself [Dm]our [Em]King [G]of [Am]Peace.
{end_of_verse}
